# PowerCore token hygiene

Save tokens by default. Full audit only when asked (`/token-audit` → skill `powercore-token-audit`).
End of substantive turns: `py -3.13 -m tools.skill_gap.endgates --auto --plain` (from agent-skills). Rank/miss metrics: `py -3.13 -m tools.skill_gap.run_rank_evals --json`.

## Do

- Keep each `CLAUDE.md` / always-on rule **short**. Prefer skills for long procedures.
- Prefer **tool deferral** / fewer MCP servers over loading every tool schema every turn.
- Subagents: **inherit** the session model unless a cheaper/faster model is explicitly set for that agent.
- Shell/hooks: rewrite noisy commands to quieter output when a PreToolUse hook exists.
- Scheduled / cron work: keep interval **≤ cache lifetime** so prompt cache can hit.

## Do not

- Paste giant docs into always-on memory (`CLAUDE.md`, alwaysApply rules) — soft caps: **~5k tokens per file**, **~10k cumulative** across layered CLAUDE.md + @imports.
- Connect unused MCP servers “just in case.”
- Auto-switch models mid-session unless the operator asked.
- Dump full MCP catalogs, session logs, or audit tables unless the operator requested an audit.

## On request

Operator says `token audit` / `/token-audit` → follow **powercore-token-audit** (report only).
